# Stage 0 - admission

Only for the NEW-task branch of "Always start here" in `SKILL.md` (`ppl recover --task
<TASK-ID>` came back `SCHEMA_INVALID`). If a run already existed, do not run `ppl init` again -
calling it on an existing run raises `ILLEGAL_TRANSITION` - and resume from the stage `ppl
show` reported; a run still in `admission` goes on from step 3 here, since the resume ran
step 2.

1. `ppl init <TASK-ID> --tracker-url <url> --harness <!-- include: harness/name -->` - the run
   takes the lane's worktree, which `ppl lane` made before this session started, and the
   harness snapshot the lane exported. A run has to exist before the task is read, because a
   fetched issue is stored in the run, and before any role is dispatched.
2. Run `<!-- include: os/ppl --> lessons pending`. <!-- include: os/flag-note --> It prints one
   `<task> <bundle>` line for each run of this harness that ended with its reflection still
   to do, and claims each for this lane, so no other lane reflects on it. Follow
   `references/reflection.md` for every line, with the bundle it names, then go on.
3. <!-- include: tracker/admission -->
4. Check the admission list: one outcome, fixed governing revision (the one step 3 names), stable and verifiable
   acceptance criteria, closed material decisions, satisfied dependencies, risk tier, a
   non-empty write boundary, enumerated forbidden paths, a proof path defined before any
   implementation, and a budget.
5. Anything missing: `ppl escalate --code SPEC_GAP --question "..."` and stop. A task that
   fails admission does not get clarified along the way by a worker.
